# Week 3 Day 1 Report

## Objective

To prepare the dataset for demand forecasting and implement a Moving Average forecasting approach.

## Data Preparation

* Converted the Date column into datetime format.
* Sorted the dataset chronologically.
* Set Date as the index for time-series analysis.

## Historical Demand Trend

A historical demand trend graph was generated using Units Sold.

### Observation

The demand data shows significant fluctuations over time with multiple peaks and drops. This indicates varying customer demand across different dates, products, and stores.

## Moving Average Forecasting

A 7-day Moving Average was applied to smooth short-term fluctuations in demand.

### Observation

The Moving Average line reduced noise in the data and highlighted the overall demand trend. Compared to actual demand values, the moving average produced a smoother representation of demand behavior.

## Sample Forecast Values

The latest forecast values were generated using the rolling average of the previous seven observations.

## Business Interpretation

* Moving Average forecasting helps identify underlying demand patterns.
* Smoothing techniques reduce short-term volatility.
* Forecasting can support inventory planning and replenishment decisions.

## Conclusion

The dataset was successfully prepared for time-series forecasting, and a 7-day Moving Average model was implemented as a baseline forecasting method. This serves as the foundation for advanced forecasting models in the next phase.
